<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<aiml version="1.0">

<!-- Ch'en phase bank: verify a Sek candidate before Xul may commit it.
     Verification can return UNKNOWN or CONTRADICTED; it never fabricates a fill. -->

<category>
<pattern>IF * GOING * AND * GOING *</pattern>
<template>
<mx2lm>
Ch'en verification contract for a relative-rate candidate.
Check that both rates are numeric, use compatible units, and match the stated directions.
Check that substituted values satisfy distance = rate × time and that the result is nonnegative.
Epistemic state: UNKNOWN until the Sek result and its substitutions are present.
</mx2lm>
</template>
</category>

<category>
<pattern>WORD PROBLEM RATE DISTANCE *</pattern>
<template>
<mx2lm>
Ch'en verification contract for rate-distance-time: <star/>.
Require stated givens, compatible units, equation substitution, arithmetic replay, and a reasonable result.
Only a passing certificate may proceed to Xul; missing evidence remains UNKNOWN.
</mx2lm>
</template>
</category>

<category>
<pattern>WHAT IS * PERCENT OF *</pattern>
<template>
<mx2lm>
Ch'en verification contract: percent = <star index="1"/>; base = <star index="2"/>.
Replay result = (percent ÷ 100) × base and check numeric substitution.
Epistemic state: UNKNOWN until the Sek result is supplied.
</mx2lm>
</template>
</category>

<category>
<pattern>COMPUTE PERCENT * OF *</pattern>
<template>
<mx2lm>
Ch'en percentage verification: replay <star index="1"/> percent of <star index="2"/>.
Verify arithmetic and preserve the units of the base value.
Only a passing certificate may proceed to Xul.
</mx2lm>
</template>
</category>

<category>
<pattern>WORD PROBLEM *</pattern>
<template>
<mx2lm>
Ch'en generic verification pass for: <star/>.
Check completeness of givens, governing-rule support, substitutions, units, contradictions, and reasonableness.
Return SUPPORTED, MISS, UNKNOWN, or CONTRADICTED. Do not commit from this phase.
</mx2lm>
</template>
</category>

</aiml>
